    <briefdescription>
<para>Persistent login session across reboots. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Lets the host keep the current login valid across a bounded number of reboots, so a device that reboots mid-session (firmware bug, watchdog) does not force a re-login. The budget is a plain reboot counter — no wall-clock/RTC is needed: each restore consumes one reboot from the budget.</para>
<para>Storage is delegated to the integrator through read/write handlers (same pattern as the command history), so the shell core stays storage-agnostic. A no-init RAM region is the natural backing store: it survives a warm reboot but is lost on real power removal.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Whoosh Embedded Team </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="copyright"><para>Copyright (c) 2025 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
